────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
(B) ACADEMIC CONTENT
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The assignment reports and coursework documents in this repository were
produced for the MSc programme "Cybersecurity and Artificial Intelligence
Technologies" at the University of Piraeus, Department of Digital Systems.

They are published here solely to document the author's academic work for
portfolio and reference purposes.

PERMITTED

  1. Reading the documents.
  2. Citing them in academic or professional work, with full attribution to
     the author(s) and a reference to this repository.

EXPRESSLY NOT PERMITTED

  1. SUBMITTING any part of this work, in original or modified form, as your
     own coursework, assignment, thesis or examination material at any
     educational institution. Doing so constitutes academic misconduct and is
     the responsibility of the person who submits it.
  2. Redistributing, republishing or hosting the documents elsewhere, in whole
     or in part.
  3. Using the documents, or content derived from them, in any commercial
     product, service, training dataset or publication.
  4. Removing or altering author attribution, institutional identification or
     supervising-faculty credits.


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CO-AUTHORED WORK
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Several documents in this repository are group assignments with additional
co-authors, who retain their own rights in that material. Where an assignment
is marked as a group project, permission to reuse it must be obtained from all
of its authors, not from the repository owner alone.

Certain coursework has been withheld from publication entirely for
intellectual-property reasons, and its absence is noted in the corresponding
entry on the site.


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
EDUCATIONAL AND RESEARCH CONTEXT
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Several documents describe offensive security techniques — including network
attacks, exploitation, malware analysis and wireless attacks. All such work was
carried out exclusively in controlled, isolated laboratory environments for
academic purposes. No real systems, networks or individuals were targeted.

This material is published for educational and documentary purposes only. The
author accepts no responsibility for any use made of the techniques described
herein against systems for which the reader does not hold explicit
authorisation. Unauthorised access to computer systems is a criminal offence in
most jurisdictions.


